    "code": "import datetime\n\n\ndef must_change_password(user: dict, today: datetime.date) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return True if the user must be forced to change their password at next login\n    under the current password rules (NIST SP 800-63B mandatory requirements only).\n    \n    Args:\n        user: dict with keys \"last_changed\" (datetime.date) and \"compromised\" (bool).\n        today: datetime.date representing the current date.\n    \n    Returns:\n        bool: True if password change is required, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # According to current NIST SP 800-63B mandatory requirements:\n    # - Password change is required if compromised.\n    # - Passwords SHALL NOT be required to change periodically.\n    # Hence, only compromised triggers a forced change.\n    return user.get(\"compromised\", False)\n",
